@page
@{ ViewData["Title"] = "Accessibility statement"; }
<div class="govuk-grid-row">
    <div class="govuk-grid-column-two-thirds">
        <h1 class="govuk-heading-l">Accessibility statement for The Share</h1>
        <p class="govuk-body">The Share is a hackathon rebuild of a casework service for the Homes for Ukraine programme. We want as many people as possible to be able to use it.</p>

        <h2 class="govuk-heading-m">How we built it</h2>
        <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
            <li>Every page uses GOV.UK Frontend components and the GOV.UK page template, including a skip link to the main content</li>
            <li>Statuses are shown as tags with words, never by colour alone</li>
            <li>Every action is a link or a button you can reach with a keyboard, with GOV.UK focus styles</li>
            <li>Wide tables scroll inside their own labelled box on small screens, so pages do not scroll sideways</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 class="govuk-heading-m">How we tested it</h2>
        <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
            <li>Automated tests check every page has a page title, exactly one main heading, a skip link and a label for every form field</li>
            <li>We checked every page with axe-core against WCAG 2.2 level AA, on a desktop screen and at phone width (390 pixels)</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="govuk-body">We have not had the service audited by accessibility specialists or tested with users of assistive technology.</p>

        <h2 class="govuk-heading-m">Known issues</h2>
        <p class="govuk-body">Following GOV.UK Design System guidance, the phase banner and back links sit before the main content area, outside a page landmark. Automated best-practice checks flag this.</p>

        <h2 class="govuk-heading-m">Data in this service</h2>
        <p class="govuk-body">All data in The Share is synthetic. Every name and record is invented.</p>
    </div>
</div>
